# `docs/` is ignored: it is mostly generated design/audit output that is deliberately
# untracked. The AI docs are the exception — they are part of the delivered feature and
# must be updatable without `-f`. Trailing `/*` rather than a bare `/docs` is what makes
# that possible: ignoring a directory outright stops git from descending into it, so no
# later negation can re-include a file inside it. Ignoring the directory's *entries*
# instead leaves the traversal open, which is what lets these two negations win.
/docs/*
!/docs/ai-golden-queries.md
!/docs/ai-load.js
